From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH v2 0/3] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:12:28 +0000

This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
the list's mail hub" [1] describes, on b/dev. It turns the relay jail
into the list's home: OpenSMTPD takes posts, Dovecot holds and serves
the list, and mbsync keeps it in sync with Fastmail.

- Patch 1 corrects the spec on what Dovecot does to a reader's write.
  A STORE or EXPUNGE answers OK and changes nothing; only append,
  copy, and move are refused. Acceptance step 7 now expects that.
- Patch 2 is the implementation as specced, with one gap: LMTP alone
  delivers only to INBOX, so a post waits there until Pat moves it
  into lists.
- Patch 3 is a proposal on top: a Sieve script from Pigeonhole files
  each post into lists, as the spec says. The spec names the new
  package and says why Sieve rather than LMTP's detail mailbox.

The tree after patch 3 is identical to v1's. What I tested, against
that tree, in a rootless Dovecot 2.3.21 run from the FreeBSD packages
the jail installs, with ports and paths moved under /tmp:
- OpenSMTPD's own mail.lmtp delivers a post into lists, with
  Return-Path and Delivered-To: lab-devel@p7x.dev added and nothing
  else changed.
- A reader login with any password gets rights "lr". SELECT opens
  lists read-only, STORE and EXPUNGE change nothing, and MOVE and
  APPEND answer NO.
- pat@p7x.dev and mbsync log in only with their imap-users password,
  in any case. Each gets "lrwstie", and Pat's MOVE to Archive works.
- The sync config against a maildir standing in for Fastmail: posts
  and Fastmail mail cross both ways, an archived message reaches
  Archive on the far side and is only marked \Deleted in its lists,
  and a quiet run logs nothing.
- The import of a jj maildir copy as Pat, as README.org gives it.
- check-message against fake filter sessions: a good message, no
  Message-ID, two From fields, a header with no empty line after it,
  an mbox "From " line, and a leading continuation line. Only the good
  message and a folded Subject pass.
- smtpd -n accepts smtpd.conf, and doveconf -n accepts dovecot.conf.

What I could not test:
- The tree after patch 2 alone. Dovecot is no longer installed here,
  so its dovecot.conf, which only drops the Sieve plugin and leaves
  delivery to INBOX, Dovecot's default, is unchecked.
- smtpd itself needs root, so the recipient sorting, the discard
  action, and the filter wiring are checked only for syntax. The same
  goes for the check script and the jail build. Steps 1 to 6 and 11 to
  13 of the acceptance test cover them.

The clients on beastie and lab-claude are not in this series. Moving
them to the hub retires the jj maildir that lab-process-mail runs on,
and the spec leaves its new loop to a spec of its own.

Changes in v2:
- Sieve moves out of the implementation into patch 3, on top, so the
  implementation matches the spec as discussed and the Sieve change
  reads as its own diff (Pat).
- The Dovecot rights correction is its own patch, first.
- Commit messages give the "what" as bullet points (Pat).
